# Surface 8-Material Taxonomy & Gatekeepers

Flat design eliminated spatial depth, while early skeuomorphism created visual clutter. Tuff introduces "sub-surface materiality" to establish lightweight yet grounded spatial order.

## Why Professional Desktop UIs Require Sub-surface Materials

Physical materiality is an intuitive cognitive anchor, not decorative garnish:
- **Spatial Continuity**: Transmitting ambient cues through translucent media preserves awareness of underlying context.
- **Depth Hierarchy**: Varying refractive indexes and blur radii immediately communicate focal boundaries.
- **Cognitive Relief**: Translucent surfaces relieve visual tension compared to monolithic solid blocks.

## The 8-Material Physical Matrix

| Surface Mode | Rendering Pipeline | Physical Metaphor | Typical Target |
|---|---|---|---|
| `refraction` (Default) | SVG Displacement Map + RGB Dispersion | Crystalline Prism | CoreBox main window, cards, dialogs |
| `glass` | Backdrop Filter Blur + Specular Inset Ring | Frosted Glass | Ephemeral menus, floating action bars |
| `acrylic` | Multi-stage Blur + Noise Scatter | Diffuse Acrylic | Sidebars, utility drawers |
| `mica` | Harmonized Wallpaper Sampling | Dynamic Mica | Root window foundation (zero GPU hit) |
| `mask` | Monochrome Translucent Alpha Mask | Ink Film | Rapid motion fallback, dense table rows |
| `blur` | Native CSS `backdrop-filter: blur(20px)` | Basic Frost | Low-tier GPU fallback environments |
| `flat` | Solid Monolithic Fill | Dense Polymer | High-contrast accessibility modes |
| `plain` | Zero Style Passthrough | Empty Space | Structural layout wrapper |

## The Absolute Rule: Default to Refraction

In the TuffEx component family, **every container component featuring a surface layer must strictly default to `refraction`**.

This establishes the visual signature of Tuff. Whether in CoreBox, modals, drawers, or cards, refraction delivers a unified, refractive aesthetic across the desktop surface.

## Explicit Confirmation Gatekeeper for Mode Switching

If a specialized scenario demands switching `surface` from `refraction` to another material (such as `flat` or `glass`):
- **Explicit manual user confirmation is mandatory**!
- Neither AI coding agents nor engineers may arbitrarily override the default material.
- This gatekeeper preserves design system integrity across distributed teams and automated workflows.
